            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "For $x(t-T_0/8)$, the common phase shift is $\\omega_0 t_0 = \\pi/4$. Subtract $2(\\pi/4)$ from the $k=2$ phase and $3(\\pi/4)$ from the $k=3$ phase; the DC term stays at $0$ and the magnitudes stay unchanged.",
